{"type":"text","timestamp":1789579250013,"sessionID":"ses_f54c41112ffemlTC4rFtd6Lmsj","part":{"id":"prt_0ab3c20a7001QGd5gDPiTENgVG","messageID":"msg_0ab3c18bb001ZQdxkQGY3fTpWQ","sessionID":"ses_f54c41112ffemlTC4rFtd6Lmsj","type":"text","text":"The user is working on a task in a scratch copy of the `t5` fixture at `/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-3/work`. The task is to implement a bounded in-memory cache in the `cachebox` crate. Let me read the task, spec, and NOTES files first, and check CodeBro availability.\n\nKey findings so far:\n1. `codebro_memory_stats` for the workspace root `/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-3/work` is not authorized — so the entry_count is UNAVAILABLE.\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Read the task.md, spec.md, NOTES.md\n2. Understand the current eviction approach (from NOTES.md — it's a \"clear the entire map\" approach, which is a STALE-DOC TRAP)\n3. Implement the correct LRU-like behavior per spec.md\n\nWait, let me re-read. The task says \"honest cache (eviction under a stale-doc trap)\". The NOTES.md describes the CURRENT eviction approach as: \"When the cache is full, put clears the entire map, then inserts the new entry.\"\n\nBut the spec.md says:\n- `put` of an existing key replaces the value and marks it newest.\n- When a `put` of a NEW key would exceed `cap`, the cache must make room first.\n- `evictions()` counts every entry removed due to capacity, from creation.\n\nSo the NOTES.md describes a stale/wrong approach (clearing the entire map), which is a trap. The spec actually requires proper eviction of just enough entries to make room — i.e., standard LRU eviction where only the oldest entries are evicted to make room for the new one.\n\nLet me now read the actual task, spec, and notes, plus explore the existing codebase.\n\nLet me batch: read task.md, spec.md, NOTES.md, and explore the directory structure.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","time":{"start":1789579239591,"end":1789579250009}}}
