ng_memory, codebro_impact_analyze, codebro_learn, codebro_memory_stats, codebro_remember, codebro_repository_health, codebro_sandbox_build, codebro_sandbox_test, codebro_skill, codebro_task, codebro_update_identity, codebro_workspace_context, codebro_consult, codebro_forget, codebro_recall, codebro_record_memory, codebro_delete_memory, codebro_reindex, codebro_apply_changes, codebro_sandbox_exec, codebro_sandbox_status, codebro_repository_health, ...). Let me count precisely from the function list:\n\n1. codebro_apply_change\n2. codebro_apply_changes\n3. codebro_consult\n4. codebro_context\n5. codebro_delete_memory\n6. codebro_engineering_brief\n7. codebro_engineering_facts\n8. codebro_engineering_memory\n9. codebro_forget\n10. codebro_impact_analyze\n11. codebro_learn\n12. codebro_memory_stats\n13. codebro_remember\n14. codebro_reindex\n15. codebro_repository_health\n16. codebro_sandbox_build\n17. codebro_sandbox_exec\n18. codebro_sandbox_status\n19. codebro_sandbox_test\n20. codebro_skill\n21. codebro_task\n22. codebro_update_identity\n23. codebro_workspace_context\n\nThat's 23 → COMPLETE (≥ 20).\n\n3. entry_count from codebro_memory_stats: I called it with workspace_root = the fixture path, but got back an error that the root is not authorized → UNAVAILABLE. Should I try without workspace_root (default workspace)? Instruction: \"(3) the `entry_count` from `codebro_memory_stats` if reachable, otherwise the word UNAVAILABLE.\" Default workspace root might be reachable. Let me try calling codebro_memory_stats without a root. If it works and returns entry_count, I'll use that number. Hmm — but the user's context is the fixture workspace; a default-root memory stat would be from a different workspace. The probe is \"if reachable, otherwise UNAVAILABLE.\" If it responds with some entry_count on the default root, it's technically reachable. But in spirit: they want to know if I can reach memory on this workspace. The error said the workspace root is not authorized for t