ed rule). T4 2/2 both (buried stdout appendix read by all; no trap-hits). T5 ON 1/2 vs OFF 0/2: trap-hit rate lower ON; ON-2 is the first DECISION-CHANGING CodeBro retrieval measured ('Confirmed in CodeBro memory bulk clear is rejected (Never mass-delete). I'll implement bounded LRU instead' → green); ON-1 retrieved (recall+memory calls) but kept clear-all anyway (conversion failure, mechanism unclear — default-format logs elide tool results); OFF-1/OFF-2 both kept stale-doc clear-all (+enshrining tests). T6 2/2 both (full spec read by all). Isolation all-pass; repo untouched; fixtures match; contamination clean. Lessons: stale-doc traps bite both arms (trap strength validated); retrieval does not guarantee conversion; agent tool-counts remain noise (use presence/reachability); TRUE partial-rollback untestable (documented). Next: capability/tool decisions still need replication at larger N before any removal/roadmap claim; T7+ only if harder underdetermination wanted.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1789579416696,"end":1789579416700}},"id":"prt_0ab3ed473001wtgo3ST7UVUCV5","sessionID":"ses_f54c41112ffemlTC4rFtd6Lmsj","messageID":"msg_0ab3ea6e6001Vfz6xR6iGnag3Q"}}
